//? Title: Stacked hourglass:visible tensor supervision on real person crops
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Use actual source-image-disjoint COCO8-Pose oracle crops and tensor Gaussian targets. Explain missing-channel-safe loss,preactivation residuals,two recursive hourglasses and learned prediction feedback. Show a visibly SGD-fitted coordinate prior and all18 Adam updates,restore separate RGB-only inference with immutable BN state,and compare every held-out joint and actual skeleton preview.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/stacked_hourglass.cpp`.

> The method

Observed RGB feeds a complete two-stack depth4 hourglass. Both raw joint heads receive explicit masked Gaussian supervision. The report owns all learned leaves,BN state,SGD reference fitting,Adam minibatches and paired validation checkpoint. Numeric crop preparation,targets,decoding,PCK and skeleton rasterization use tensors;original source identities keep the tiny data experiment interpretable.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/stacked_hourglass_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/stacked_hourglass_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/stacked_hourglass_concept.tikz > build/stacked_hourglass_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/stacked_hourglass_concept.svg build/stacked_hourglass_concept.dvi > build/stacked_hourglass_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
