> Gaussian supervision respects original annotation support

COCO visibility1 and2 both supervise;visibility0 is missing,not a zero-location
label. Map input-pixel coordinates to heatmap centers with
(x+.5)*side/input_size-.5. Unnormalized Gaussians truncate each axis at3*sigma.
Out-of-image or nonfinite positions produce a masked zero channel. Target
construction uses detached tensors,so these coordinates are not optimized.
The border fixture preserves truncation rather than renormalizing kernel mass.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stacked_hourglass_gaussian.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto joints = n::tensor({41.5, 81.5, 2., 0., 127., 1., NAN, NAN, 0.}, {1, 3, 3});
  const auto targets = m::PoseHeatmaps(joints);
  const auto decoded = m::DecodePoseHeatmaps(targets.heatmap);
  std::print("Visibility1+2 active;missing NaN support0. Decoded target coordinates:{}\n",
             decoded);
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(
           n::reverse(n::select(n::select(targets.heatmap, 0, 0), 2, 0), {0}), 0, 1),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(
           n::reverse(n::select(n::select(targets.heatmap, 0, 0), 2, 1), {0}), 0, 1);
  a.title("Interior half-pixel Gaussian")
      .x_label("heatmap column")
      .y_label("heatmap row0 at bottom");
  b.title("Border Gaussian retains truncation")
      .x_label("heatmap column")
      .y_label("heatmap row0 at bottom");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/stacked_hourglass_gaussian.svg");
}
```
