> Missing channels cannot contaminate the loss

Each image first averages MSE over its own annotated joint channels and
all spatial pixels. Then supported images have equal weight. Empty images
are excluded;all-empty input gives a graph-connected zero. Select missing
predictions and targets out before subtraction,so their NaNs and gradients
cannot leak. The hand fixture has two annotated channels with error2,one
channel with error3,and a third empty image:loss=(4+9)/2=6.5.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stacked_hourglass_masked_loss.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto mask = n::tensor({1., 1., 1., 0., 0., 0.}, {3, 1, 1, 2}),
             values = n::tensor({2., 2., 3., NAN, NAN, NAN}, {3, 1, 1, 2}),
             active = n::greater(mask, .5);
  const auto p = (n::ones({3, 2, 2, 2}) * values).requires_grad_(),
             truth = n::where(active, n::zeros_like(p), n::full(p.shape(), NAN)),
             loss = m::PoseHeatmapMSE(p, truth, mask, 2), gradient = n::grad(loss, {p})[0];
  std::print(
      "Equal supported-image MSE {:.6f};all gradients finite:{};missing adjoint max {:.3g}.\n",
      loss.item(), n::all(n::is_finite(gradient)).item<bool>(),
      n::max(n::where(active, 0., n::abs(gradient))).item());
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(mask.reshape({3, 2}), {0}), 0, 1),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(n::mean(gradient, {1, 2}), {0}), 0, .75);
  a.title("Original image/joint supervision")
      .x_label("joint channel")
      .y_label("source image0 at bottom");
  b.title("Exact per-pixel channel adjoints")
      .x_label("joint channel")
      .y_label("source image0 at bottom");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/stacked_hourglass_masked_loss.svg");
}
```
