> Preactivation bottlenecks and feedback connect both stacks

A residual block applies BN/ReLU before1x1/3x3/1x1 convolutions with a
half-width bottleneck. Its skip is identity or a1x1 projection;there is no
activation after addition. Each hourglass combines a same-scale upper
residual with a pooled recursive lower path and nearest upsampling.
Two stacks receive separate heatmap supervision. Learned feature and
prediction projections feed the next stack,so final loss also differentiates
the earlier predicted head. BN moving state is explicit and separate.

Full256px,width256/stem64 and compact128px,width32/stem8 both retain depth4,
two stacks and17 linear output channels. Native checks execute full backward,
all396 learned tensors,RGB gradients and the feedback derivative. The
following compact graph prints all14 retained stages and checks the actual
final-head derivative with respect to the first head.
```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::print("| graph | learned values | leaves | BN values | BN leaves | stages "
             "|\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (bool compact : {false, true}) {
    const auto config = compact ? m::CompactHourglassConfig() : m::HourglassConfig{};
    n::ParameterStore p(173), state(179);
    const auto image = n::full({2, config.size, config.size, 3}, .4);
    if (!compact) {
      n::NoGradGuard guard;
      const auto out = m::StackedHourglass(p, state, image, config);
      std::print("| full | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", p.count(), p.size(), state.count(),
                 state.size(), out.stages.size());
    } else {
      const auto out = m::StackedHourglass(p, state, image, config, true, false);
      const auto feedback = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(out.heatmaps[1])), {out.heatmaps[0]})[0];
      std::print("| compact | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\nFinal-head loss -> first-head "
                 "derivative norm {:.6f}.\n| stage | H | W | C |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n",
                 p.count(), p.size(), state.count(), state.size(), out.stages.size(),
                 n::sqrt(n::sum(n::square(feedback))).item());
      for (std::size_t i = 0; i < out.stages.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i + 1, out.stages[i].size(1),
                   out.stages[i].size(2), out.stages[i].size(3));
    }
  }
}
```
