> Genuine COCO8-Pose crops and a visibly SGD-fitted reference

Prepare the pinned official341,756-byte COCO8-Pose archive with
dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("pose"). Original train image IDs36/49/77 fit;86 validates.
Original validation images110/113/136/151 are held out. Person boxes expand
1.25 independently in each axis,then integer-floor/ceil clipped cropping and
legacy bilinear128px resizing use tensors. Joint transforms and original box
extents use the same crop geometry;label coordinates clamp to0..127.
These are **ground-truth person crops**,not detections. Fitting-only width
reversal also swaps anatomical left/right identities and maps labeled x to127-x.
The manifest retains all original files,person IDs,crop bounds and mirrors.

```{cpp, flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("pose", (cache / "human_pose").string());
}
```
// result_begin:
// result_end

The12 fitting rows are six people from three photographs plus mirrors.
Validation is one person/one image;test has14 people from four photographs.
Multiple people from one image are dependent. Every original crop RGB pixel,
annotation,box transform and anatomical mirror is checked independently.
All12 fitting crops and original annotated skeletons are shown.

Fit a per-joint coordinate reference with one explicit Double SGD(.5) step
on summed per-joint mean squared error. Joints absent from fitting get a
fixed63.5 center target. The closed-form tensor mean is only a parity oracle.
Save the visibly fitted prior;the training example later loads it unchanged.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/stacked_hourglass_data.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";

  std::filesystem::path root = cache / "human_pose";
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_POSE_DIR"))
    root = p;
  else
    dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("pose", root.string());
  const auto split = m::LoadPoseCrops(root);

  const auto known = n::greater(n::slice_axis(split.fit.joints, 2, 2, 3), 0.),
             weight = known.to(n::DType::Float64),
             xy = n::where(known, n::slice_axis(split.fit.joints, 2, 0, 2), 0.)
                      .to(n::DType::Float64),
             counts = n::sum(weight, {0});
  n::ParameterStore prior(181, n::DType::Float64);
  const auto parameter = prior.get("coordinates", {17, 2}, n::init::zeros());
  n::OptimizerConfig options;
  options.kind = n::OptimizerKind::Sgd;
  n::Optimizer sgd(prior, .5, options);
  const auto error = n::sum(weight * n::square(parameter - xy), {0}) /
                     n::maximum(counts, n::ones_like(counts)),
             fallback = n::where(n::equal(counts, 0.), n::square(parameter - 63.5), 0.);
  sgd.minimize(n::sum(error + fallback));
  const auto mean = n::concat({parameter.detach().to(n::DType::Float32), n::ones({17, 1})}, 1);
  const double parity = n::max(n::abs(mean - m::FitPoseMean(split.fit))).item();
  if (parity > 2e-5)
    return 1;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  n::save_npz("build/stacked_hourglass_sgd_prior.npz", {{"pose", mean}});
  const auto targets = m::PoseHeatmaps(split.fit.joints);
  const auto tiles = m::PosePreviewTiles(split.fit, split.fit.joints, targets.heatmap);
  n::save_image_grid(n::slice_axis(tiles, 2, 0, 256), "figures/stacked_hourglass_inputs.png",
                     2, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1);
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const std::array<dm::graphics::RGB, 3> colors = {
      {{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}, {22, 163, 74}}};
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::string, m::PoseData>> data = {
      {"fitting", split.fit}, {"validation", split.validation}, {"test", split.test}};
  int offset = 0, index = 0;
  std::print("One visible SGD(.5) coordinate update;closed-form parity {:.3g};{} fitting "
             "joints unsupported.\n| split | crops | annotated joints |\n|---|---:|---:|\n",
             parity, n::count_nonzero(n::equal(counts, 0.)).item<std::int64_t>());
  for (const auto &item : data) {
    const auto supported =
                   n::greater(n::select(item.second.joints, 2, 2), 0.).to(n::DType::Float64),
               per = n::sum(supported, {1});
    a.points(n::arange(offset, offset + per.numel()).to_vector<double>(),
             per.to_vector<double>(), item.first, colors[index++]);
    offset += per.numel();
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", item.first, per.numel(), n::sum(per).item<int>());
  }
  a.title("Actual original annotation support")
      .x_label("prepared split crop order")
      .y_label("labeled COCO17 joints per crop")
      .y_limits(0, 23);
  b.bars(n::arange(0, 17).to_vector<double>(), counts.to_vector<double>(), "fitting support",
         {147, 51, 234})
      .title("Observed joints fitting the SGD prior")
      .x_label("COCO17 joint index")
      .y_label("labeled fitting crop count")
      .y_limits(0, 16);
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/stacked_hourglass_data.svg");
}
```
