\image(figures/stacked_hourglass_training.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All18 visible Adam updates supervise both recursive heads. Validation uses moving BN while the fixed fit probe uses batch BN;paired parameter/BN files restore the same selected epoch.)
\alttext(All18 visible Adam updates supervise both recursive heads. Validation uses moving BN while the fixed fit probe uses batch BN;paired parameter/BN files restore the same selected epoch.)


\image(figures/stacked_hourglass_metrics.svg)
\caption(All116 annotated joints in14 oracle crops/four original test photographs compare learned final-head positions with a visibly SGD-fitted coordinate prior and fixed crop center. PCK is inclusive and joint-weighted;this is not COCO keypoint AP.)
\alttext(Held-out joint-weighted PCK and actual crop-pixel errors for learned,SGD and fixed-center predictions.)

\image(figures/stacked_hourglass_predictions.png)
\caption(All14 actual held-out person crops,two tiles per row. Each tile is observed RGB,green original annotated skeleton,red unthresholded predicted skeleton,and red/blue maximum linear heatmap clipped only for display. Continuous-distance tensor rasterization changes display edges only.)
\alttext(Original held-out COCO8-Pose person crops,ground-truth and predicted skeletons,and actual final-head heatmap maxima.)

The learned final head reaches PCK.103448,below the SGD prior.172414.
It exceeds the fixed center’s.068966 PCK,but its mean joint error
66.137554 pixels is worse than both SGD41.032688 and center46.302833.
Thus the short fit does not demonstrate improved localization over the
fitting-only reference,and different diagnostics do not give identical rankings.

A reduced fitting objective does not establish accurate joint localization.
Compare learned positions against both references and inspect every actual
crop. Oracle boxes,limited source-image independence,a single validation
person and three short epochs sharply limit the quality claim. The report
preserves mechanisms and measurable errors rather than paper benchmark accuracy.

> Conclusion

Independent target/loss/residual/decoder/metric Jacobians and full/compact graph checks establish the mechanisms. Real source-image-disjoint crops support a visible SGD reference and every intermediate-supervision Adam update. Immutable RGB-only inference and complete held-out joint/skeleton comparisons bound this tiny teaching fit’s accuracy claims.

> References

- [Newell,Yang and Deng,Stacked Hourglass Networks for Human Pose Estimation](https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.06937).
- [Original Torch recursive model and prediction feedback](https://github.com/princeton-vl/pose-hg-train/blob/master/src/models/hg.lua).
- [Official COCO8-Pose dataset definition and source archive](https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/blob/main/ultralytics/cfg/datasets/coco8-pose.yaml).
- [Lin et al.,Microsoft COCO:Common Objects in Context](https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.0312).
